### 4.3 Off-grid generalization check

To test that grid-based validation is not self-serving, all tiers were
re-checked at deliberately unseen conditions (4 fuels: CH4 baseline and the
three error-prone ones C2H2, C3H8, nC4H10; IDT at φ = 0.7/1.3, P = 3/20
atm, T0 = 1150–1750 K — 64 points; SL at φ = 0.7/1.3/1.5, Tu = 350 K,
P = 2 atm — 12 points; none of these φ/P/T/Tu values appear in the
validation grid). Raw outputs in `results/offgrid/`, comparisons
`results/cmp_offgrid_*.json`:

| tier | IDT mean/max % | SL mean/max % |
|---|---|---|
| L | 0.61 / 4.4 | 0.27 / 0.7 |
| M | 0.87 / 3.8 | 0.49 / 1.3 |
| S | 1.56 / 5.4 | 1.11 / 3.5 |

All off-grid errors are inside the a-priori tolerances, i.e. the delivered
